==============================================================================
DRIVE taper SHAPE — real small-signal gain vs knob (existing ladders, no new capture)
==============================================================================
220 Hz fundamental at [-60, -57, -54, -51] dBFS (clean regime); gain = |H1_out| - A_in (dB).
Model: R=100k*(1-x)^2.5, gain=1+330k/(3.3k+R+1k). Both normalised to their OWN drive-min.

   drive |  CAP gain  MDL gain (rendered) | MDL analytic | CAP-spread MDL-spread
     min |    -12.94    -21.38            |        12.39 |       0.00       0.00
    9:30 |    -11.66    -20.85            |        17.18 |       0.00       0.00
    noon |     -7.83    -18.61            |        24.09 |       0.00       0.00
    2:30 |     -1.34    -12.00            |        33.15 |       0.00       0.00
     max |      5.44     -7.66            |        37.81 |       0.01       0.00
  (spread = max-min gain across the 4 clean levels; >~0.5 dB = clipper grazing, read is
   not fully linear there — expected at max drive.)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GAIN STEPS between adjacent knob positions (dB) — the taper SHAPE, capture vs model
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
           step |  CAPTURE    MODEL | diff (cap-mdl)
      min->9:30 |     1.29     0.53 |          +0.76
     9:30->noon |     3.83     2.24 |          +1.59
     noon->2:30 |     6.48     6.61 |          -0.12
      2:30->max |     6.78     4.35 |          +2.43

  Largest capture-vs-model step disagreement: +2.43 dB at 2:30->max.

  ** BLEED CONFOUND — READ CAREFULLY (found session 15). ** These captures are base-OD, so
  the output FUNDAMENTAL carries the drive-INDEPENDENT clean BLEND bleed (session 7/8). At
  drive-min the OD path is weak (~4x gain) and the bleed sits ABOVE it (~+7 dB), so the
  low/mid-drive gain reads are DOMINATED BY THE BLEED, not the OD drive gain — the min->9:30
  and 9:30->noon steps are NOT clean taper measurements and must NOT be over-read. Only the
  HIGH-drive steps (2:30->max, where OD dominates the bleed) are bleed-free and reliable.
  The model render carries the SAME bleed, so cap-vs-mdl partially cancels it, but only
  within the ~1-4 dB the bleed MODEL itself is uncertain (session 8).

  So the ROBUST finding here is the 2:30->max discrepancy: the real pedal's drive gain
  rises ~2.4 dB MORE at the top than the (1-x)^2.5 power law (which saturates as R->0).
  That is real, bleed-free evidence the taper SHAPE is wrong at the top — consistent with
  VR3 being a C-taper the power law approximates badly. The NOON-level question this probe
  CANNOT answer cleanly (noon fundamental is bleed-confounded); the case for the taper at
  NOON rests on the session-15 HARMONIC grids (gm — a UNIFORM level scale — does NOT fix
  noon H3-H2, so a NON-uniform level change, i.e. the taper SHAPE, is the remaining lever).
  ** Session 16 needs a BLEED-AWARE taper measurement** (subtract the drive-independent
  bleed, or measure level-into-clipper via a bleed-free route) to nail the mid-drive shape;
  then model VR3 as a proper C-taper (not (1-x)^p) and re-run the branch-B fit.
